        "name": "USN-8644-3",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - File systems infrastructure;   - OCFS2 file system;   - B.A.T.M.A.N. meshing protocol;   - SCTP protocol;   - TIPC protocol; (CVE-2026-43071, CVE-2026-52914, CVE-2026-52993, CVE-2026-53043, CVE-2026-53224, CVE-2026-53246, CVE-2026-53309)",
